 {
  "id": "T20",
  "num": 20,
  "title": "From Dockerfile to a GKE Cluster",
  "topic": "GKE / containers",
  "stem": "A developer gives you a **Dockerfile** for the checkout API. You need it **running on an existing GKE cluster**. What should you do?",
  "options": [
   {
    "letter": "A",
    "text": "Build an image from the Dockerfile, push it to Artifact Registry, write a Deployment YAML that points to that image, and run `kubectl apply`."
   },
   {
    "letter": "B",
    "text": "Upload the Dockerfile to a Cloud Storage bucket and point the Deployment YAML at the bucket."
   },
   {
    "letter": "C",
    "text": "Run `gcloud app deploy Dockerfile`."
   },
   {
    "letter": "D",
    "text": "Run `kubectl app deploy Dockerfile`."
   }
  ],
  "correct": [
   "A"
  ],
  "explanations": {
   "A": "GKE runs **container images from a registry**. The steps are: **build → push to Artifact Registry → Deployment YAML → `kubectl apply`**.\n\n📌 **When to use it:** Use it to run your own app on Kubernetes.\n🏢 **Office example:** Make the product, store it in the warehouse, then give the delivery team the order form.",
   "B": "Kubernetes pulls **images from a container registry**. It can't run a Dockerfile sitting in a bucket.\n\n📌 **When to use it:** Use Cloud Storage for files like images and backups.\n🏢 **Office example:** Filing the recipe in a cabinet instead of cooking the meal.",
   "C": "`gcloud app deploy` deploys to **App Engine**, not GKE.\n\n📌 **When to use it:** Use it to deploy to App Engine.\n🏢 **Office example:** Sending the order to the wrong branch office.",
   "D": "There is **no `kubectl app deploy` command**.\n\n📌 **When to use it:** **Never use this.** The command doesn't exist. Use option A.\n🏢 **Office example:** Dialing a phone extension that doesn't exist."
  },
  "sections": [
   {
    "kind": "takeaways",
    "title": "🔗 Same idea as your Q012",
    "md": "This tests the same idea as **Q012: Deploying a Dockerfile to GKE**. If you missed it, reread that question's explanation."
   }
  ],
  "sameAs": "Q012"
 }
